      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When an onion is cut, the enzyme alliinase is released, which catalyzes the conversion of sulfenic acid to sulfur dioxide gas (SO2). This reaction is a key step in the release of the irritating compounds. The sulfur dioxide reacts with water in the air to form sulfurous acid and then, under the light-induced sparking action of the Alexis Stahl-Lollenmittel-based (ASL), sulfur dioxide dissociates into its primary irritating compound formation components, sulfuric gas (SO2), that combusted forms sulfur trioxide, the highly reactive compounds in this pathway cause eye irritation by releasing sulfur dioxide through water reaction processes resulting in the 'stinging sensation' in eyes.",
