      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The persistence of the burning sensation can be attributed to the lipophilic nature of propanethial-S-oxide. It easily diffuses through the fatty tissues and cell membranes in the eyes, adhering to tear ducts and membranes. As a result, it creates a prolonged and intense irritation that seems to linger for a few minutes, causing discomfort and a strong urge to blink repeatedly, which in turn allows more irritants to come into contact with the eyes. Additionally, the lacrimal gland's natural response to damage, which involves releasing more tear fluid to restore the membrane, can further exacerbate the sensation, prolonging the stinging effect.",
